sections.4.body:
Consultancies and agencies are known for long hours in busy periods. GOV.UK explains that you [can't work more than 48 hours a week on average](https://www.gov.uk/maximum-weekly-working-hours), normally averaged over 17 weeks, unless you choose to opt out, and that employers need to keep some records about working hours.

Paidlyo isn't designed as a working time compliance system. It doesn't record clock-in and clock-out times, breaks or rest periods, and it isn't a substitute for the records your HR or payroll process keeps. Check with an HR adviser what records apply to your staff.

What Paidlyo can do is make heavy weeks **visible**. If people track all their working time, billable and non-billable, the hours reports show who's consistently working long weeks and which clients or projects are driving it. That's useful for:

- spotting burnout risk before someone hands in their notice;
- rebalancing work across the team;
- having an honest conversation with a client whose project is taking far more time than agreed;
- pricing future work so the hours fit a normal week.

To make this work, ask people to track internal time too, not just billable hours. A week that shows 32 billable hours might really have been 50 hours at the desk, and only the full record shows it.
